      "question": {
        ":question/id": "3fcdfdfc-02d3-5240-acf8-6d2463fd38f7",
        ":question/problem": "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{3}{16 x^{2} + 25}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=\\frac{4 x}{5}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{4}{5})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n16 x^{2} + 25=25\\left(1+(\\frac{4 x}{5})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{5}{4}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{3}{25}\\cdot \\frac{5}{4}=\\frac{3}{20}$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{3}{16 x^{2} + 25}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{3}{20}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the supplied primitive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{20}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\frac{3}{20}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{20}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{4 x}{5} \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$",
